# Fos (fos-system) — Agent Rules

## IDENTITY
- Product name: **Fos**
- Repo: `Flash1315/fos-system`
- Separate sellable product. NOT Ride & Joy branded. NOT part of RJ-Spending-bot.
- Never couple Fos to Google Sheets, Telegram chat IDs, or RJ bot internals.
- RJ may become a tenant/customer later via API — not by merging codebases.

## MAIN RULE
Make only surgical, targeted changes. Never rewrite entire functions or files.

## FORBIDDEN
- Rewriting existing functions entirely
- Changing code unrelated to the current task
- Removing existing logic without explicit instruction
- Changing monorepo structure (`api/`, `mobile/`) without explicit ask
- Adding new imports unless required for the task
- Mixing Fos with RJ-Spending-bot or deploying Fos into `/root/rjbot`
- Hardcoding a single-company workflow (always multi-tenant by `organization_id`)
- Skipping approval flow for money records unless explicitly asked
- Storing plaintext passwords

## ALLOWED
- Adding new lines inside existing functions
- Fixing specific logic surgically
- Adding new functions at end of file
- Changing only what the task specifies
- New API routers/modules when the task requires a new domain

## CODE STYLE
- Language: **English only** (UI strings, comments, commits, docs in repo)
- Mobile: every multi-step flow must have **Back** and **Cancel**
- Log server errors via `print()` (or structured logger if already present)
- API responses and schema field names: snake_case JSON matching existing patterns
- Password hashing: `pbkdf2_sha256` via passlib (do not switch back to bcrypt without cause)

## ARCHITECTURE (do not violate)
- `api/` — FastAPI + SQLAlchemy, JWT auth, multi-tenant
- `mobile/` — Expo (React Native) TypeScript client
- Tenant isolation: every business query filters by `user.organization_id`
- Roles: `owner` | `manager` | `employee`
- Money kinds: `expense` | `fuel` | `income`
- Record status: `pending` → `approved` | `rejected` (managers/owners decide)
- Cash on hand (v1): approved `income` with `payment_method=cash` − approved `expense` − approved `fuel` (per user)
- Login requires `organization_slug` + email + password
- Local DB default: SQLite; Postgres via `DATABASE_URL` only

## PRODUCT SCOPE GUARD
- v1 in scope: orgs, invite, roles, expense/fuel/income, approvals, cash on hand, Expo shell
- Out of v1 unless explicitly asked: photo→S3/R2, web admin/billing, Telegram bridge, FX, white-label, GPS, calendar/CRM from RJ

## COMMITS / PRS
- Branch names: `cursor/<descriptive-name>-e418` when using Cursor cloud agents
- Prefer small commits; English commit messages
- Do not invent RJ notification routing rules here — they do not apply
